# Make a rogue who is wearing the Springblade Bracers, in a frozen dungeon.
#
# Included by springblade-cold.keys, springblade-hot.keys and
# springblade-jam.keys, which differ only in what they do afterwards.
# bd inc-tek.8.8, finding PA-08-F14.
#
# WHY A ROGUE. The item's own page says rogues are who it is for, and the
# Handle Device check the fix adds is a rogue skill. A barbarian would jam on
# every attempt and could never deploy, so no run could measure the second
# half.
#
# THE BRACERS ARE MADE IN WIZARD MODE, because Item "springblade" and the
# effect that carries it both sit behind IT_NOGEN (lib/m_items.irh) and no
# walk can find a pair.
#
#   w y                    enter wizard mode
#   Wizard Mode Switches   Freeze Monsters, so that nothing retaliates. A blow
#   DOWN*10 SPACE          landing on the wielder would zero his own FFCount
#                          and quietly change what the second half measures.
#   Item Acquisition       the acquisition browser
#   RIGHT*21               walk the glyph row to Bracers. ItemGlyphs
#                          (src/Tables.cpp:320-345) puts -AI_BRACERS 21 steps
#                          along, and the header line names the category, so a
#                          miscount shows up in a dump as some other word after
#                          "Acquisition -- [...]:".
#   @until ... DOWN        the candidate list has no menu letters, so the
#                          cursor is walked instead. The window shows three
#                          rows and highlights the middle one, so the run stops
#                          on the pass where the row BELOW the wanted one first
#                          appears. That is an ordering assumption about
#                          lib/m_items.irh; the checks do not trust it and read
#                          the item's name back off the activate menu first.
#   ENTER r SPACE ENTER    take it, put it in the Bracers slot, leave the
#                          inventory manager.

@include chargen-rogue.keys

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play

w
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes

w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN*10
SPACE   # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES
ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*21
@until "Devilbane Bracers" DOWN
ENTER
r
SPACE
ENTER
